# Patch:        040-tower-inherent-repr
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       binary-field/src/clmul/mod.rs, binary-field/src/extension.rs, binary-field/src/gf2.rs, binary-field/src/poly_basis.rs, binary-field/src/subfield.rs, binary-field/src/tower.rs
# Hunks:        7
# Class:        equiv-rewrite
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 9: every tower level reaches the level
#               below through `TowerLevel::{from_repr, to_repr, mul_alpha}`, and
#               `TowerLevel: Field` pulls in p3-field's trait hierarchy. Without
#               this patch aeneas stops: "Mixed-recursive declaration groups are
#               not supported".
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the copies are compiled but unused there.
#               In the extracted variant, inherent `from_repr`, `to_repr` and
#               `mul_alpha` shadow the `TowerLevel` methods at every call site on a
#               concrete level, and call copies with the trait methods' bodies.
#               `Gf2`'s copies build the value directly: `from_bool((r & 1) == 1)`
#               is `Self(r & 1)`, and `u8::from(self.is_one())` is
#               `(self.0 == 1) as u8`.
# Upstreamable: no: the shims exist only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    aeneas accepts p3-field's trait hierarchy (issue 9).
# Test:         test p3-binary-field --lib pre_patch_040
# Mutation:     `raw_mul_alpha` swaps the coefficients it joins, so the copy and
#               `TowerLevel::mul_alpha` disagree from `GF(2^4)` up.
#
# The tower's arithmetic reaches the level below through `<$lower>::from_repr`,
# `to_repr` and `mul_alpha`.
# Those are `TowerLevel` methods, and `TowerLevel: Field`, so reaching one reaches
# the level's `Field`, `PrimeCharacteristicRing` and `Div` impls.
# aeneas rejects that group (issue 9), so no tower arithmetic was extracted.
# Each level, and `Gf2`, now has `raw_from_repr`, `raw_to_repr` and
# `raw_mul_alpha`, compiled in every build.
# Under cfg(hax_backend_lean), inherent methods named like the trait methods call
# them, and Rust resolves an inherent method before a trait method, so no call site
# changes.
# The differential test compares each copy with the trait method: exhaustively up
# to `GF(2^16)`, on edge values and 10000 pseudo-random inputs above.
# The `TowerLevel` imports that the shims leave unused are allowed under the cfg.
#
